-- Targeted ingestion (2026-09-03): bibliographic data only, NOT tagged --
-- 23 books the repo owner (Mathias) named as titles he remembers reading
-- and rated (loved/liked/disliked/hated), confirmed missing from the
-- catalog by checking against local first (see below for the ones that
-- turned out to already be present). Each hardcover_id below was
-- confirmed via a search-only pass first, not auto-matched -- generated
-- from scripts/_scratch-gen-migration.js's run against local (not
-- committed, a one-off scratch script; see docs/project-log.md for the
-- per-book confirmation notes).
--
-- Already in the catalog, so NOT re-inserted here (bibliographic data
-- only, ratings handled separately in data/ratings/mathias.json):
--   - Valor (John Gwynne, Faithful and the Fallen #2, hardcover_id
--     478363) -- confirmed already present.
--   - Ender's Shadow (Orson Scott Card, hardcover_id 264175) -- already
--     present AND already rated 'loved'.
--   - The Shadow of What Was Lost (James Islington, Licanius #1,
--     hardcover_id 445584) -- already present AND already rated 'liked'.
--   - The Light of All That Falls (James Islington, Licanius #3,
--     hardcover_id 441085) -- already present but NOT yet rated; rating
--     added to mathias.json, no insert needed here.
--   - Kings of Paradise (Richard Nell, hardcover_id 433544) -- already
--     present and already rated 'loved'; deliberately not touched.
--     Note: its series_id is NULL (Hardcover's own record for this book
--     also has no featured_series), so it's NOT linked to the new
--     'Ash and Sand' series row created below even though its two
--     sequels are -- flagged in project-log.md as an optional follow-up
--     for the repo owner, not fixed here since fixing an existing row
--     wasn't asked for.
--
-- Disambiguations worth noting explicitly:
--   - "Valor" is John Gwynne's (Faithful and the Fallen #2), not Brian
--     McClellan's -- per repo owner's own correction.
--   - "The Malice" (hardcover_id 481926, Peter Newman, The Vagrant #2)
--     is a DIFFERENT book from "Malice" (hardcover_id 429071, John
--     Gwynne, Faithful and the Fallen #1) already in the catalog --
--     confirmed distinct hardcover_id/author/series before inserting;
--     both titles now coexist.
--   - "I'm Afraid You've Got Dragons" was named as Peter McLean's but is
--     actually Peter S. Beagle's (2024, hardcover_id 1086185) -- no
--     Peter McLean book by this title exists on Hardcover (searched
--     directly, and confirmed via cached_contributors on every
--     candidate id). Treated the same way as the Valor/McClellan
--     correction above: trusted the title match over the misattributed
--     author. Flagged for the repo owner in case this isn't actually
--     the book he meant.
--   - "The Wandering Inn": Hardcover represents this ongoing web serial
--     as many individual volume entries plus one primary series entry.
--     Picked hardcover_id 446694 (title "The Wandering Inn", the
--     highest-popularity entry, users_count 903, tagged as series
--     position #1) as the single representative entry per the task's
--     instruction to prefer one sensible entry over adding dozens of
--     volumes -- not the "(Web)" variant volumes, which are a separate,
--     lower-popularity parallel listing of the same content.
--
-- Author-field contamination stripped (narrator names dropped, per
-- CLAUDE.md's data-quality section) before inserting:
--   - "Prince of Fools" (hardcover_id 159149): Hardcover's author_names
--     included "Tim Gerard Reynolds" (audiobook narrator) -- inserted
--     as 'Mark Lawrence' only.
--   - "Blackwing" (hardcover_id 445518): Hardcover's author_names
--     included "Colin Mace" (audiobook narrator) -- inserted as
--     'Ed McDonald' only.
--
-- New series created (hardcover-sourced): Ash and Sand, The Lot Lands,
-- Covenant of Steel, Iconoclasts, The Vagrant, Empire of the Wolf,
-- The Wandering Inn, The Red Queen's War, Raven's Mark, Time Master,
-- Impossible Times.
--
-- Deliberately NOT rated in data/ratings/mathias.json even though
-- inserted here: "One Word Kill" (Mark Lawrence, Impossible Times #1,
-- hardcover_id 427996) -- the repo owner said only "didn't resonate
-- well with me", which doesn't map unambiguously to one of the 5 rating
-- labels (disliked vs it_was_okay are both plausible). Bibliographic
-- data added so it's ready to tag/rate once he specifies which.
--
-- Deliberately NOT added at all (sequels not asked for): Iconoclasts
-- #2/#3 (only Aching God was named), Raven's Mark #2+ (only Blackwing
-- was named), The Vagrant #3 "The Seven" (only books 1-2 were named).

